    "text": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented a bounded stack with comprehensive tests. Here's what was created:\n\n## BoundedStack Class\nLocated in category **'BoundedStack'** with the following methods:\n\n**Factory method:**\n- `capacity:` \u2014 Creates a stack with a given positive integer capacity; validates the capacity and raises error if invalid\n\n**Core operations:**\n- `push:` \u2014 Adds an object on top; raises \"stack is full\" if at capacity\n- `pop` \u2014 Removes and returns the top object; raises \"stack is empty\" if empty\n- `top` \u2014 Returns the top object without removing it; raises \"stack is empty\" if empty\n- `isEmpty` \u2014 Returns true if the stack contains no elements\n- `size` \u2014 Returns the current number of elements\n\n**Initialization:**\n- `initializeCapacity:` \u2014 Internal initialization method\n\n## BoundedStackTests Class\nLocated in category **'BoundedStack-Tests'** with 15 comprehensive tests covering:\n\n\u2705 Invalid capacity validation (zero, negative, non-integer)  \n\u2705 Valid stack creation  \n\u2705 Push and pop operations  \n\u2705 Top without removing  \n\u2705 isEmpty and size tracking  \n\u2705 Full stack errors with correct message  \n\u2705 Empty stack errors for both pop and top with correct messages  \n\u2705 LIFO (Last-In-First-Out) behavior  \n\u2705 Multiple push/pop cycles  \n\n**All 15 tests pass.** The image has been saved and is ready for you to review. The packages are unsaved and ready to file out when you're ready."
